🧠 ui_styleguide.mdc – Lash Studio Design Brain

description: Modular design reference for a high-end beauty salon site. Tailored for Cursor AI, this governs typography, colors, spacing, motion, and UX patterns to ensure consistency across all pages.

🎨 Typography System
Fonts

Fraunces (serif) → Headlines / Display (emotional, elegant)

Manrope (sans) → Body / UI text (clean, modern)

Roles
Role	Use Case	Notes
Display	Hero headlines, big banners	Fraunces, tight tracking
Headline	Section titles	Fraunces, strong contrast
Title	Cards, small blocks, modals	Fraunces bold, compact
Body	Paragraphs, descriptions	Manrope, relaxed line-height
Label	Buttons, captions, form labels	Manrope, medium weight
✍️ Typesetting Rules

Scale & spacing:

h1 → text-5xl md:text-6xl font-serif tracking-tight

h2 → text-3xl font-serif

h3 → text-xl font-serif

p → text-base leading-relaxed text-ink/70

Vertical rhythm: 24 / 32 / 40px multiples for consistent flow

Whitespace: generous margins around headlines and CTAs to keep it airy and premium

🎨 Color System
Palette

Blush Rose #EEDDE2 (soft background accent)

Mauve #D9C2C8 (secondary UI, tabs)

Porcelain #FAF8F7 (default background)

Charcoal Ink #1C1A1A (main text)

Champagne Gold #CFB27C (accents, rules, subtle CTAs)

Usage

Background: Porcelain

Primary text: Ink

Accent (buttons, separators): Gold

Do not overuse blush/mauve — keep as highlights

⚡ Motion & Interaction

Entrance: Fade + rise (200–300ms, ease-out)

Stagger: 60–80ms between elements

Hover: Slight lift (scale 1.01, shadow deepen)

Tap: Bounce spring (framer-motion)

Accessibility: Respect prefers-reduced-motion

Animations should be subtle, editorial, elegant, never distracting.

♿ Accessibility & Contrast

Large text min contrast 3:1

Small text min contrast 4.5:1

Links must be clearly styled (underline or distinct color)

Form elements require <label> and ARIA tags

Locale switcher must be keyboard accessible

🧠 UX Laws (Applied for Booking UX)

Hick’s Law: Keep booking steps minimal (2–3 taps)

Fitts’s Law: Big CTA buttons, sticky mobile booking bar

Miller’s Law: Don’t overload with too many services at once; chunk by category

Peak-End Rule: Booking confirmation should feel delightful (toast + summary)

Occam’s Razor: Only necessary fields in forms (name, phone, service, master)

Tesler’s Law: Shift complexity (deposits, no-show fees) to provider logic, not UI

✅ DOs & DON'Ts

✅ Keep whitespace generous — editorial, not cramped

✅ Use serif for impact, sans for clarity

✅ Use brand tokens only (no ad-hoc hex colors)

✅ Always show booking policies clearly (deposit, cancellation)

⚠️ Don’t over-animate

⚠️ Don’t stack multiple decorative fonts

⚠️ Don’t hide essential booking info behind clicks

📦 Tokens & Spacing
--font-display: 'Fraunces', serif
--font-body:    'Manrope', sans-serif

--color-bg:      #FAF8F7
--color-text:    #1C1A1A
--color-accent:  #CFB27C
--color-blush:   #EEDDE2
--color-mauve:   #D9C2C8

--space-xs: 4px
--space-sm: 8px
--space-md: 16px
--space-lg: 24px
--space-xl: 40px
--radius-xl: 20px
--radius-2xl: 24px
--shadow-card: 0 10px 24px rgba(28,26,26,0.08)
🎯 Key Takeaways

Luxury through simplicity → airy layout, serif headlines, gold accents.

Low-friction booking → fewer steps, clear policies, big CTAs.

Consistency → same rhythm, same tokens, same components (shadcn).

Elegance, not overload → subtle motion, restrained palette.

✅ This styleguide now “teaches” Cursor to always design/build in a premium salon aesthetic: editorial typography, airy layouts, blush/gold tones, and smooth booking UX.